        "original_id": "2ba5cd6e-d9ab-5e3d-9985-cefacbadd7f3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Richard Llewellyn, Saki, Hector Hugh Munro\n- Works: Green, Green My Valley Now, When William Came\n- Roles: British novelist, British writer, author\n- Topics: Pen names, Edwardian society and culture\n\nFacts:\n- Hector Hugh Munro, better known by the pen name Saki and also as H. H. Munro, was born on 18 December 1870 and died on 14 November 1916.\n- Saki was a British writer whose witty, mischievous, and sometimes macabre stories satirized Edwardian society and culture.\n- When William Came: A Story of London Under the Hohenzollerns is a novel by Saki, the pseudonym of Hector Hugh Munro, and it was published in November 1913.\n- Richard Dafydd Vivian Llewellyn Lloyd, known by his pen name Richard Llewellyn, was born on 8 December 1906 and died on 30 November 1983.\n- Richard Llewellyn was a British novelist.\n- Green, Green My Valley Now is a 1975 novel by Richard Llewellyn.",
